osition":{"commit_sha":"bcde06f02b046e199dfba0e62ad4ff2ac25efc9b","position":"1795183387807926083-84144f77-8ec4-4076-b096-9ec58b8b6971"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"e40e14b53f301b8963dce2d78eb005b3efadb03b0082a42843e8374d385bf5b4","event_uuid":"d4cf505b-a7de-4175-acee-1871e781f290","position":{"commit_sha":"18ad8f0c7f51bc6787ad893ae73a076a99b5ebb8","position":"1795188723123134001-d4cf505b-a7de-4175-acee-1871e781f290"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIMQNvvCya66a6YyDlxwkxjjJPN3uaFI+QD3OjyC8e1UF rebar-mac-492a5c71 joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com 20261119"},{"content_hash":"94ebbfe97122a70ce983dc6afca86e0d5687dd263faa140bce940b5245e4b9e3","event_uuid":"04105475-17ae-4f81-96e6-ee5577cd6130","position":{"commit_sha":"e8e41c0492876a1474bad07a40f05905098df66e","position":"1795189570046389489-04105475-17ae-4f81-96e6-ee5577cd6130"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"},{"content_hash":"bff6a6b0b0f549f73dc52d3a6b9d8a8286b3d754442c5bec6e6bb1f8f2b4a1b2","event_uuid":"a526cd3d-4bc6-4f0c-87c4-c9f1d66a28bb","position":{"commit_sha":"79989cb749540b0a7e70160904c266f1a0a15fd6","position":"1795192092550579357-a526cd3d-4bc6-4f0c-87c4-c9f1d66a28bb"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIGNNmnI/WYNJAOKH9yvo0l+tMYJR2tK2UV4H8ReXBQU5 rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com rotated-20260907"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-311_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"05f74084-8156-4489-b43f-fbb9222cdc20","comments":[{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Blocked on design (no code changed, not claimed): the MCP op-cert signer reads the same setting as authorship. src/rebar/mcp_server.py compose_startup_opcert_binding() builds the startup op-cert signer from cfg.identity.signing_key (REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY) plus REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID, and main() binds it for every certified tool. Pointing REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY at /run/secrets/rebar-bot-signing-key would make plan-review and completion-verifier certs sign with the bot key under env 9f1c8e42-..., which is not in REBAR_VERIFY_TRUSTED_OPCERT_KEYS. tests/unit/test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py (around line 152) pins that coupling. Separating the two keys needs a code change to the op-cert key source (e.g. read REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH, which the opcert service already uses), awaiting operator decision.","timestamp":1795140503854703001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"review-plan PASS (signed at 717c50f8b33). Acting on 2 advisories within scope: (a) when MCP composes its box op-cert signer (REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID set), startup also validates the authorship key named by identity.signing_key with the same keyprov checks (exists, regular, 0600, valid Ed25519) and fails closed, preserving today's posture where an empty/invalid key stopped startup; no new config. (b) Setting REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH in the MCP container also points the unbound op-cert fallback in _opcert_signing at the same op-cert key instead of the tracker genesis key; intended, same key as the bound signer. Not acted on: blast-radius advisory about the MCP container holding the bot key; that is the operator's recorded decision.","timestamp":1795143141102700001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Implemented in local commit fb9aaec0adf (not yet pushed): compose_startup_opcert_binding reads REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH; startup fails closed with REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID set and a missing/invalid op-cert key or an unset/unusable authorship key; compose mcp service + autodeploy mcp_run_new set REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH=/run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key, REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY=/run/secrets/rebar-bot-signing-key and mount rebar-bot-signing-key :ro. Red evidence: 7 goose tests fail against unmodified mcp_server.py. Mutation check: signing authorship with the op-cert key makes the new verify-identity test fail with 2 signer-not-on-keyring. make verify running.","timestamp":1795144180916938001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Pushed Gerrit change 3476 (patch set 1, 01e0dcfa3e1, rebased on origin/main 2ca3e28fcc6). Main's 2ca3e28fcc6 goose fail-closed tests were adapted to set REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH plus a separate authorship key; the too-permissive authorship case skips on Windows per cloistered-decomposed-nymph. make verify (9h46m on a load ~37 host) caught one of mine (broad except flagged by test_tombstone_registry; fixed by validating the authorship key before composing the signer). On the rebased tree my modules, typecheck and lint pass; 7 unrelated tests still fail (incl. known-red test_reclaim_resign), comparison against origin/main running.","timestamp":1795182461002529001},{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Patch set 2 (a25f1b77913) on Gerrit 3476. PS1 got LLM-Review +1 and Verified -1; CI failed only on test_reclaim_resign (main breakage, gloomful-genial-pronghorn) on all 3 Linux cells. PS2 addresses advisories: the authorship-key startup check no longer reuses the Ed25519-only op-cert validator (now: regular file, 0600 on POSIX, ssh-keygen -y loads it passphrase-free; any key type, no temp copy), bare pytest.raises got a match, runbook notes a blank bot-key slot stops MCP startup. Confirmed the bot key on identity 594c's keyring (fingerprint oGCqzgfDMpDX...) is ssh-ed25519. fetch-secrets.sh wording advisory not taken: editing it redeploys review-bot too. Will rebase once the main fix lands.","timestamp":1795188723123134001}],"created_at":1795123784877533001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"8c0460a1-875f-4647-8f2a-5cf08f928afa","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"df01-290f-89a2-4ce8"},{"link_uuid":"ed0792fa-02ef-4a51-9613-a7918caf359b","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"8983-a808-7ad5-4d20"},{"link_uuid":"84144f77-8ec4-4076-b096-9ec58b8b6971","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"471b-7c16-87b1-4e17"},{"link_uuid":"04105475-17ae-4f81-96e6-ee5577cd6130","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0e5d-73f7-a01c-4322"},{"link_uuid":"a526cd3d-4bc6-4f0c-87c4-c9f1d66a28bb","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"2c6e-d3ef-7183-4d21"}],"description":"## Observation\nThe MCP server signs every event it writes with its op-cert key. `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` and `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` (`mcp_run_new`) set `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY=/run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key` for the MCP container, and `_apply_authorship` (`src/rebar/_commands/_seam.py`) signs each MCP-written event with that key under principal 594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d. Identity 594c's keyring does not hold that key, so since starving-sphalerite-skua (Gerrit 3460) each such event classifies `signer-not-on-keyring` and fails enforced `verify-identity`. On the tickets history that is 6,101 verdicts from 2 op-cert keys, and every new MCP write adds another.\n\nRoot cause of the coupling: `compose_startup_opcert_binding` (`src/rebar/mcp_server.py`) builds the MCP server's op-cert signer from `cfg.identity.signing_key`, which is the same setting authorship signing reads. One variable therefore selects both keys, so the authorship key cannot change without changing the op-cert key.\n\n## Operator decision (made)\nMCP authorship signatures use the rebar bot signing key (`/rebar/prod/rebar-bot-signing-key`, already on identity 594c's keyring and already used by the `review-bot` service). The op-cert key keeps signing op-certs. No keyring or SSM change. The op-cert key path comes from the existing `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` variable, which the `opcert` service and the unbound signing seam (`src/rebar/_opcert_signing.py`) already read.\n\n## Approach\n1. `compose_startup_opcert_binding(cfg)` reads the op-cert key path from `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` and no longer reads `cfg.identity.signing_key`. It reuses `rebar.opcert_service.keyprov.compose_signer` with `OpcertServiceConfig(env_id=..., key_path=...)` unchanged, so key validation (exists, regular file, 0600, valid Ed25519) is the existing code. Behaviour: `REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID` unset -> `None` (developer/stdio path, unchanged). `REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID` set and `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` unset -> `compose_signer` raises `OpcertKeyError` and startup fails closed, so a box that claims an environment can never silently fall back to the tracker genesis key. A bad key file also fails closed, as today. The new read site carries `# mechanism-ok: env_var REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH \u2014 promising-unwasteful-xantus` and the `# read-via: credential-deployment-override` tag used at the other read sites; the mechanism baseline is not hand-edited. Regenerate `docs/env-vars.md` with `scripts/gen_env_registry.py`.\n2. MCP container env, in both `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` (`mcp` service) and `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` (`mcp_run_new`): `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH=/run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key`, `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY=/run/secrets/rebar-bot-signing-key`, plus a read-only bind mount `./rebar-bot-signing-key:/run/secrets/rebar-bot-signing-key:ro` (compose) / `-v \"$COMPOSE_DIR/rebar-bot-signing-key:/run/secrets/rebar-bot-signing-key:ro\"` (autodeploy), matching the `review-bot` service. Keep the op-cert key mount.\n3. Deployment: `infra/scripts/fetch-secrets.sh` already writes `rebar-bot-signing-key` (0600) next to `.env`, and autodeploy's MCP path runs it with `ENV_FILE=$COMPOSE_DIR/.env` before `mcp_run_new`, so the file the new mount names exists on the box with no manual step. No change to fetch-secrets.sh, terraform, SSM, or any keyring.\n4. Docs: update `infra/runbooks/mcp-opcert-enforcement-flip.md` (preconditions and Related section describe the op-cert key as selected by `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY`) and any other doc that names the shared setting for the MCP service.\n\n## Scope\nIn: the op-cert key source for the MCP startup signer, the MCP container env/mounts in compose and autodeploy, the tests that pin them, the env registry doc, the runbook. Out: the `opcert` service, the `review-bot` service, `_apply_authorship`, fetch-secrets.sh, terraform, SSM parameters, keyrings, rewriting the 6,101 historical events (they remain as recorded). No new config key, env var, or flag: `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` already exists and `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY` only changes value.\n\n## Testing\nTests first, in `tests/unit/test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py`:\n- With `REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID` + `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` = op-cert key and `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY` = a different (bot) key, the composed binding's public key equals the op-cert key's and not the bot key's (fails on current code, which composes from the bot key).\n- With `REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID` set and `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` unset (only `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY` set), `compose_startup_opcert_binding` raises `OpcertKeyError`.\n- With both keys configured, an event written through the library write seam under a bound op-cert signer carries `author_sig` from the bot key (the authorship key), not the op-cert key; and a completion-verifier cert minted through the binding verifies against the pinned op-cert key (existing round-trip test, switched to `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH`).\n- Existing goose tests (`_compose_binding`, bad-key fail-closed) switch to `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH`.\nIn `tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py` (and the compose parity test in `tests/unit/test_opcert_deploy_infra.py` if it pins the mcp env): the composed MCP env defines `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY` exactly once with value `/run/secrets/rebar-bot-signing-key`, defines `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH=/run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key`, and compose and `mcp_run_new` agree on both values and both mounts.\nThen `make verify` before push.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Unit test: with `REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID` set, `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` naming the op-cert key, and `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY` naming a different key, the binding from `compose_startup_opcert_binding` signs with the op-cert key's public key.\n- [ ] Unit test: with `REBAR_OPCERT_ENV_ID` set and `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` unset, `compose_startup_opcert_binding` raises `OpcertKeyError`.\n- [ ] Unit test: an event written while the op-cert binding is active carries an `author_sig` whose signer is the `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY` key.\n- [ ] Unit test: a completion-verifier op-cert minted through a binding composed from `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` passes `verify-opcert --require-environment` (exit 0).\n- [ ] Parity test: the `mcp` service in `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` sets `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH=/run/secrets/opcert-ed25519-key`.\n- [ ] Parity test: the `mcp` service in `infra/compose/docker-compose.yml` sets `REBAR_IDENTITY_SIGNING_KEY=/run/secrets/rebar-bot-signing-key`.\n- [ ] Parity test: the `mcp` service mounts `./rebar-bot-signing-key` read-only at `/run/secrets/rebar-bot-signing-key`.\n- [ ] Parity test: `mcp_run_new` in `infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh` passes the same 2 env values as the compose `mcp` service.\n- [ ] Parity test: `mcp_run_new` mounts `$COMPOSE_DIR/rebar-bot-signing-key` read-only at `/run/secrets/rebar-bot-signing-key`.\n- [ ] `python scripts/gen_env_registry.py --check` exits 0 with the regenerated `docs/env-vars.md`.\n- [ ] `infra/runbooks/mcp-opcert-enforcement-flip.md` names `REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH` as the MCP op-cert key source.\n- [ ] `make verify` exits 0 on the change before push.\n- [ ] The Gerrit change reaches LLM-Review +1 with Verified +1 and is merged to origin/main.\n- [ ] After autodeploy, one new event written through the MCP server classifies `verified` under `verify-identity` with `REBAR_IDENTITY_REQUIRE_AUTHENTICATED=1`.","env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/mcp_server.py","reason":"op-cert startup signer reads REBAR_OPCERT_KEY_PATH instead of identity.signing_key"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_mcp_opcert_signing_goose.py","reason":"tests for key separation and fail-closed startup"},{"path":"tests/scripts/test_autodeploy_mcp_bluegreen.py","reason":"composed MCP env parity for the two key variables"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_opcert_deploy_infra.py","reason":"compose parity for mcp env and mounts, if pinned there"},{"path":"infra/compose/docker-compose.yml","reason":"mcp service env and bot key mount"},{"path":"infra/scripts/autodeploy.sh","reason":"mcp_run_new env and bot key mount"},{"path":"infra/runbooks/mcp-opcert-enforcement-flip.md","reason":"describe the separate op-cert key variable"},{"path":"docs/env-vars.md","reason":"regenerated env registry (new read site)"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","managed_refs":[["relates_to","0e5d-73f7-a01c-4322"],["relates_to","2c6e-d3ef-7183-4d21"],["relates_to","471b-7c16-87b1-4e17"],["relates_to","8983-a808-7ad5-4d20"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"2be1098e-4322-4742-9090-b49ae2867a68","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"releases":[],"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"97f7-b448-9cdb-47ce","ticket_type":"bug","title":"MCP server signs events with its op-cert key, which is not on the author's keyring","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["a73198f3-c1d8-4ecc-9def-8df24121e5f0","3e14749a-432b-4063-b64f-78889601bd9b","797e1296-7c3d-4fe9-86e6-501efb73c6f5","ed0792fa-02ef-4a51-9613-a7918caf359b","1baf138c-5162-45dd-9a06-ffc05b6a3e21","97eb7f32-3057-4133-9d87-3332760991ff","2be1098e-4322-4742-9090-b49ae2867a68","7ec65d1f-457d-49b4-bd19-671914cf50d5","9047b878-9ff2-4b5f-8d29-17c9b66d7909","a9237a43-edd3-443b-8856-57ba6f756dac","4acfb182-f4ef-40cc-9b53-a2b715aede10","84144f77-8ec4-4076-b096-9ec58b8b6971","d4cf505b-a7de-4175-acee-1871e781f290","04105475-17ae-4f81-96e6-ee5577cd6130","a526cd3d-4bc6-4f0c-87c4-c9f1d66a28bb"]},"env_id":"","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1795192092550579358,"uuid":"17cab55e-d600-4368-b8be-b277d8655c4b"}
